1
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:15,931
The cultural festival we'd spent
so long preparing and rehearsing for,

2
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:18,309
came and went in the blink of an eye.

3
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,853
Did you take that carpet home?

4
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,604
Nah, man. Why would I take your costume?

5
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:23,522
And the very next day...

6
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:24,691
Aw, what a waste.

7
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:32,699
MOMOKA, TODAY
IT'S BEEN A WHILE

8
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,702
Sorry, I know it was random.

9
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:38,496
But I wanted to talk to you,
Madame Koyun.

10
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,625
Yeah. Me too.

11
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,546
What'd you wanna talk about?

12
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,715
I guess I'll get straight to the point.

13
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,843
I would like you to stay
away from Minato.

14
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,068
{\an8}THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

15
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:30,942
EPISODE 21
MISUNDERSTANDINGS

16
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:36,114
I'm always full of contradictions,
I know. But I can't help it.

17
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:40,617
I kept telling myself "don't worry,
she's not a threat."

18
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:43,705
But the idea of her, her
very presence drove me nuts.

19
00:02:44,747 --> 00:02:46,457
I just... hate her so much.

20
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,794
I checked in with her first,
so many times.

21
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,172
I gave her every opportunity.

22
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:56,050
If she liked him, she should've
jumped while she had the chance.

23
00:02:56,593 --> 00:03:00,179
For her to suddenly try to
cozy up to him now... It's disgusting.

24
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,055
- Okay.
- Huh?

25
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:03,975
I'll keep my distance from Amamiya.

26
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:06,352
To clarify,

27
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:09,229
you mean you just weren't a
fan of us hanging out together,

28
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,398
even in a group, right?

29
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:12,065
Or are you saying

30
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:14,694
you want me to stop
talking to him completely?

31
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:17,488
Um... I guess, I...

32
00:03:18,114 --> 00:03:20,199
Cause if that's the case, it
might be pretty hard

33
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,785
since we're in the same class and
will run into each other every day.

34
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:25,997
I don't wanna be flat-out rude to him.

35
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,456
Well,

36
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:31,461
I guess you and Amamiya can let me know
whether or not it feels rude to you.

37
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,213
It depends on how Minato feels about it?

38
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:35,215
Is that...

39
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:38,968
because you're just so sure
he'll choose you over me?

40
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:43,389
Why is she acting like it's no big deal?
Like she doesn't even care?

41
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:46,601
Even though I'm his girlfriend,

42
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:48,811
the one standing in her way.

43
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:51,981
And you're okay with it?

44
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:53,524
Just like that?

45
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:57,737
Madame Koyun
I know you've always denied it

46
00:03:58,529 --> 00:04:00,490
but you have a crush on him, don't you?

47
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:04,284
Look, whether or not
I have feelings for Amamiya

48
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:06,329
has no bearing on your relationship.

49
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,790
It doesn't change who he's dating.

50
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,084
The one he chose is you, Momoka.

51
00:04:12,835 --> 00:04:16,338
I'm sorry if I gave you any reason to
feel suspicious about anything,

52
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:17,298
but

53
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:21,009
you have nothing to worry about,
cause since you started dating

54
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,052
I can promise you

55
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:24,514
he's only treated me as a friend,
nothing more.

56
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:28,601
I think he's genuinely trying to
be in a relationship with you.

57
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,229
Whatever you may have thought

58
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:33,147
he and I are just friends.

59
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,733
But if you still feel
like you can't trust me,

60
00:04:36,734 --> 00:04:40,405
then I won't go near Amamiya, if doing
that would make you uncomfortable.

61
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:43,032
All I'm asking in return

62
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:44,659
is that you trust him.

63
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:48,162
Why?

64
00:04:49,163 --> 00:04:52,332
When I directly asked you if you
liked him, you didn't deny it.

65
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:53,959
That's your answer right there.

66
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,961
{\an8}YOU COULD AT LEAST LET IT SHOW

67
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:59,340
{\an8}YOU'RE CLEARLY NOT HAPPY ABOUT IT
YOU'RE CLEARLY NOT HAPPY ABOUT IT

68
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:01,926
It's as though...

69
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,345
I'm the one at fault or something.

70
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:09,225
Even though I had the decency to
talk it out face-to-face.

71
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:12,602
Well, that's good to hear.

72
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:15,355
That you're rational enough to
stop pursuing someone

73
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:17,567
once he's gotten himself a girlfriend.

74
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,067
Yeah, we're dating.

75
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:22,447
But it's not a binding agreement
or marriage or anything like that.

76
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:25,282
Nothing more than a verbal agreement, really.

77
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:26,825
I'M NOTHING MORE THAN SOMEONE HE'S DATING

78
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:30,580
I can't help but worry when you and
Minato are together. It's only natural.

79
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:34,499
Because I know if it were me,
I probably would've kept trying.

80
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,626
Even if the guy I liked had a girlfriend.

81
00:05:36,627 --> 00:05:38,045
THE CAUSE OF MY ANXIETY...

82
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:40,298
I would've never given up
on him that easily.

83
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:45,177
I'm not gonna let someone who doesn't
seem to really care either way...

84
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,179
I DEFINITELY

85
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,306
LOVE HIM MORE

86
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:50,224
steal him from me.

87
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:55,937
You'd "keep trying?"

88
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,773
- As in...?
- Huh?

89
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:58,857
Yeah,

90
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:02,194
it's true things turned out this way
cause of just how hard you tried.

91
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:03,111
But...

92
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:06,406
if you keep trying even though
your crush likes someone else,

93
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:07,742
wouldn't that be selfish?

94
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:12,079
I mean, if I claim to care for someone, I
would never force my feelings on him like

95
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:12,996
that.

96
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,749
Whatever, you can't hold back
cause of everyone else.

97
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,377
Or else you're gonna lose out.

98
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:18,795
Well...

99
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:22,382
I guess it doesn't really
matter what I think, does it?

100
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:26,886
It's not like there's a point for us
to try and understand each other.

101
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:28,971
Oh... hostility.

102
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:30,514
Like...

103
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:34,559
The way you always just walk
right up to anyone without hesitation

104
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:37,145
How you're able to easily make
friends that help you achieve

105
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:40,524
whatever you want.
and how you're able to act so impulsively

106
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,567
That's a malicious way of putting it.

107
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:43,985
Really? Another lecture?

108
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:46,072
From the bottom of my heart, I've always...

109
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:48,908
envied and wanted to be more like you.

110
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:51,076
Huh?

111
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:54,079
How you can take action and
make your own choices.

112
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,249
And just how confident
you are in yourself.

113
00:06:56,749 --> 00:06:58,626
You're like the polar opposite of me.

114
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,585
And I've always been

115
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:02,754
I don't know, kinda jealous of you.

116
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,297
You're jealous of me?

117
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:05,341
Seriously?

118
00:07:05,967 --> 00:07:08,344
Oh yeah, I envy you. A lot in fact.

119
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:12,306
But in the end, I still can't
manage to bring myself to act like you.

120
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:14,100
And why is that?

121
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:17,145
Well for example,
when you interact with people

122
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:20,397
you probably draw a clear line between

123
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:23,025
those you want to get
close to and those you don't.

124
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:25,445
Well... You kinda have to.

125
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:29,449
If I gave everyone the same
level of enthusiasm, I'd get burned out.

126
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:30,949
Yeah.

127
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,201
That perspective
makes a lot of sense to me.

128
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:34,245
But still...

129
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:36,456
Momoka...

130
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:40,625
You know how she's been hanging around
you a lot recently out of nowhere?

131
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:42,962
Before that, she used to come around me.

132
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:46,048
Do you realize... what she wants?

133
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:50,011
You can't sort people by their usefulness

134
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:53,222
and treat those you
don't care about as pawns.

135
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,057
What are you even talking
about right now?

136
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,018
Did I do something...

137
00:07:57,518 --> 00:08:00,271
to hurt your feelings or give
you the wrong impression?

138
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:01,938
It's alright.

139
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:04,358
You don't have to
pretend to care about me.

140
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:06,443
It's just that...

141
00:08:06,444 --> 00:08:09,070
even those people
you're not interested in

142
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:10,907
the ones you see as pawns,

143
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:15,453
are still people with feelings
and anxieties, who can get hurt

144
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,788
the exact same way you can.

145
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,875
Even if you hide it really well

146
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:24,170
people can still tell
they were being used

147
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,005
and it hurts a lot.

148
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:27,798
You don't have to care

149
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,592
but that doesn't mean you
should treat people

150
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,261
like they don't matter at all.

151
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:35,389
That's what I wanted to tell you today.

152
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:42,562
Ahh...

153
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,397
HEH

154
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:46,149
You really have it in for me, huh?
That was quite a speech.

155
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:49,612
Well, I'm used to girls not liking me
so I'm not bothered.

156
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:51,280
That's not it.

157
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:54,534
I don't hate you or anything
if that's what you think.

158
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,035
I mean,

159
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,662
to be honest I don't know you well enough

160
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:00,122
to say one way or another.

161
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:02,917
- Annd you don't know me.
- Huh?

162
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:04,751
It's just that

163
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:08,923
there are some actions and behaviors I've
noticed that I just can't get behind.

164
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:12,510
Well hey,
thank you for pointing that out.

165
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,302
But,

166
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:17,138
in the end,
aren't our actions and behaviors

167
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:19,267
what decides if we get to
be happy or not?

168
00:09:20,184 --> 00:09:22,103
You have to "Be kind to everyone."

169
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:24,104
And "Be considerate"

170
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:25,022
they say.

171
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:27,942
Sorry, but... I don't think I can do that.

172
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:30,987
I'm not a nice person.

173
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:35,908
I can't do that well either, honestly.

174
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:37,576
But

175
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:40,871
if you only act with yourself in mind,
it'll leave you empty

176
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:43,624
obsessing over all
the things you don't have.

177
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:47,295
And I think you'll ultimately
be less happy.

178
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:50,840
Are you sure

179
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,675
this isn't about yourself?

180
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:55,303
Or are you trying to say all that to me?

181
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:57,096
To us.

182
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:58,514
So all I want

183
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,224
is for the two of you

184
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:03,686
to have a real relationship
where you can both be happy.

185
00:10:05,229 --> 00:10:06,564
- I-
- Which means

186
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:08,649
I'll keep my distance from him.

187
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:11,319
Would that make you feel better?

188
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:14,405
Yeah.

189
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,744
Man, I really hate her.

190
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:21,996
I hate her.

191
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:24,707
So her actions, her very existence,

192
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,877
every little thing annoys me to no end.

193
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:30,504
Honestly,

194
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,048
I'd prefer it if she was straight up.

195
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:36,135
Said "I hate you," to my face, and
ignored my very existence.

196
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,387
If only she were my enemy...

197
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,307
Then I could wage war
with her in my head.

198
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,310
Then I could feel completely justified.

199
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:47,563
I was the one who won...

200
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:50,566
so why do I still feel so empty?

201
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:55,820
That's what I'd
been saying the whole time.

202
00:10:55,821 --> 00:10:58,574
And then that's when
Hayato turns and says:

203
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:01,243
POUT

204
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:02,870
Momoka?

205
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:07,124
What's the matter?

206
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:12,838
Minato...

207
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,341
Would you say you liked me?

208
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:19,595
Yeah. I like you.

209
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:21,054
What do you like?

210
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:23,973
Hmm... How you're strong, and positive,

211
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:24,891
and super smart?

212
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:28,521
That's not exactly something you'd
normally say to compliment a girl.

213
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,980
It makes me sound so calculating.

214
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:31,898
I AM, BUT...

215
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:32,733
Huh?

216
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:34,944
But those were good qualities.

217
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:37,488
Then...

218
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,491
Who do you like more me or Koyun?

219
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,994
Wait, what? Me and Koyun are just friends.

220
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:46,621
So it's a different kind of "like,"
you know?

221
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:48,374
Like how I like Miki and Yota.

222
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:49,916
Okay, but what if-

223
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:53,670
what if Madame Koyun walked up to you
and said she had feelings for you?

224
00:11:53,671 --> 00:11:56,256
If she did
you'd totally choose her, wouldn't you?

225
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,425
No, I wouldn't.

226
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:00,302
Cause I'm not dating her, I'm dating you.

227
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:05,641
It's just because we're dating...

228
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:08,352
What am I missing here?

229
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:12,314
I feel like I'm doing
everything I possibly can

230
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:14,315
and yet, inevitably...

231
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:15,443
GO AHEAD

232
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,654
What are you so worried about?

233
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,657
Sorry for making you worry.

234
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,368
How can I make you stop worrying?

235
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,413
Just tell me. Say it.
What can I do to fix it?

236
00:12:29,206 --> 00:12:31,709
Stop trying to logic your
way out of this, Minato!

237
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,710
This is about feelings.

238
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:35,880
I want to know what your
real feelings are.

239
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:40,633
Fine.

240
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:42,844
Then I want you to
keep your distance from her.

241
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,763
I don't care if you say
you're just friends.

242
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,306
You guys are too close.

243
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:48,392
I can't stand how well you two get along!

244
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:53,522
You got it.

245
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,735
But like, how much distance do you mean?

246
00:12:58,235 --> 00:13:01,738
You mean you just weren't a big fan
of us hanging out together, right?

247
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:05,116
Or are you saying you want me to
stop talking to her completely?

248
00:13:05,117 --> 00:13:08,286
{\an8}Cause that'll be a lot harder since
we're in the same class and all.

249
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:09,204
{\an8}DÉJÀ VU...

250
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,123
{\an8}And will run into each other every day

251
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:17,254
Uh- Uh- Uh? What's wrong?

252
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:23,843
Oh,

253
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:25,762
your dad just said
he doesn't need dinner.

254
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,765
Well, I sure wish he had told me sooner.

255
00:13:28,891 --> 00:13:31,560
Minato, be a good boy
and eat this for me, would you?

256
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:33,437
Uh...

257
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:35,189
Sure.

258
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:39,735
I can't finish.

259
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:41,236
What?

260
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,781
But you'd normally
wolf it down in ten seconds.

261
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:45,783
Something...

262
00:13:46,575 --> 00:13:47,535
Hurts...

263
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,291
I can't sleep.

264
00:13:57,461 --> 00:14:00,214
Being in a real relationship is so hard.

265
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:04,175
I want to know what your
real feelings are.

266
00:14:04,176 --> 00:14:06,094
I'm so glad you're my friend.

267
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,178
So, thank you.

268
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,931
Someday, when you finally
fall in love with someone...

269
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:13,142
Well man, I hope one day you
feel that way about someone.

270
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:14,520
What do you really want?

271
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:24,530
Hold on...

272
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:26,866
How do I sleep again?

273
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:33,038
I don't feel like I slept
at all last night.

274
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:34,831
You know, Minato.

275
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:37,584
You've been grinding your teeth
at night a lot lately.

276
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:38,501
Huh?

277
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,670
Maybe you're stressed out
about something?

278
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:41,714
Who, me?

279
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:46,050
Maybe not.
You've always been the chill one.

280
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:46,886
Mm.

281
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:51,682
Lately, things have been feeling really...
off.

282
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:54,435
Especially this nagging
feeling in my head...

283
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:57,353
Ow...

284
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:58,938
- Agh.
- Huh? What is it?

285
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:00,441
Ah- Wait, I can't-

286
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:02,151
Minato?

287
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:04,153
It... hurts...

288
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,071
Are you okay, Minato?

289
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:08,699
Just... just hold on!

290
00:15:09,658 --> 00:15:11,076
You're just stressed out.

291
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:12,953
Stressed out?

292
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:16,624
Mm hm.
Stress shows up for everyone differently.

293
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:20,001
Sometimes it's a cumulation
of various small stressors

294
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:22,588
that you don't even register
on a conscious level.

295
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:24,923
Either way,

296
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:27,383
your mind is just overwhelmed
and exhausted.

297
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:29,928
I'll prescribe you some meds
and we'll go from there.

298
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:31,638
But if it doesn't get any better

299
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:34,265
you might want to try some
psychosomatic therapy.

300
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:35,935
Psychosomatic?

301
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:39,854
Well, good thing I didn't
have class til the afternoon today.

302
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:40,689
Yeah.

303
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,398
Minato,

304
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:44,817
you should take better care of yourself, okay?

305
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:45,819
Ugh...

306
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,365
Stress? From what?

307
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:53,535
Oopsie! Still had the parking break on.

308
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,583
Well, I made it home.

309
00:16:00,584 --> 00:16:02,043
But can I park it now?

310
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:03,087
Can I do it?

311
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:05,756
Minato, you should go inside without me.

312
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,466
Okay...

313
00:16:11,428 --> 00:16:13,138
Huh? The door's unlocked.

314
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:14,640
Why?

315
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:17,851
Ah, crap!

316
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:19,853
Oh-

317
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:21,772
Oh, it's just you, Minato.

318
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,400
Wait... Kaito?

319
00:16:28,487 --> 00:16:30,947
- Sorry to scare ya.
- Seriously?

320
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:33,908
You shouldn't be sneaking
in here like a common burglar.

321
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,995
Don't be rude. I grew up here.

322
00:16:36,537 --> 00:16:38,997
I'm curious though when I opened the door

323
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:40,915
why'd you look startled and say "crap"?

324
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,835
Oh, that. That's cause...

325
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:44,877
I was tryna take this with me.

326
00:16:44,878 --> 00:16:45,838
That's stealing!

327
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,799
It's my seal for the bank account
I opened back when I lived here.

328
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:50,925
Ugh.

329
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:54,345
I don't really care.
I have to head to campus for class so...

330
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:55,180
Do whatever.

331
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,515
I will!

332
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:59,183
Oh! And Minato's not feeling well

333
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:01,936
today, so you better not
keep him from getting rest!

334
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:03,229
Oh? He's not?

335
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,440
Yeah,
we just came back from the hospital.

336
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,399
But-

337
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,984
I'm totally fine now though.

338
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,028
Bye!

339
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:14,408
- Well, see ya.
- See you.

340
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,286
It's weird seeing you two not fight.

341
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:19,830
Hey, we're not kids anymore.

342
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:23,166
So are you like sick? What's going on?

343
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,417
Nah.

344
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,294
I'm fine now.

345
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:28,672
I guess...
I was probably just a little tired.

346
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:32,509
The doctor basically said I
"shouldn't let stress build up."

347
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:33,969
Ah...

348
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:35,636
Oh?

349
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:39,348
Well, yeah with your personality,
I'm not surprised you got so stressed.

350
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:41,435
- Huh?
- I mean c'mon.

351
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:44,896
You sacrifice listening
to your own feelings

352
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:46,774
to focus more on reading the room.

353
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,359
You try so hard not to rock the boat

354
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,861
you keep everything all
bottled up inside.

355
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:54,030
- Uh...
- You've always been like that.

356
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:54,990
Wait, that's not-

357
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:56,617
I'm sorry.

358
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:59,243
But, I know why though.

359
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:02,705
You grew up watching me constantly
get chewed out by our parents.

360
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:04,833
So I became a cautionary tale.

361
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:09,087
About how doing whatever I wanted
made me unwelcome in the family.

362
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,423
Of course that's what
you took away from it.

363
00:18:12,132 --> 00:18:15,301
You were the only one in this
house who was ever on my side.

364
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:17,679
But I kept putting you
in the middle of it.

365
00:18:18,972 --> 00:18:20,849
I made you put up with all that crap.

366
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:22,684
Sorry.

367
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,145
Where is this coming from?

368
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:30,149
I never assumed you cared or thought
deeply about others feelings.

369
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,360
Hey.

370
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:33,319
Well, I do.

371
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:37,240
And I've watched quite a few friends
of mine get so chronically stressed out.

372
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:39,200
They couldn't even work anymore.

373
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:42,412
They all suddenly snap one day
and just completely break down.

374
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:44,832
I don't want you to end up like that.

375
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:48,669
Well, I'm still a long way
from entering the workforce.

376
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:50,254
Yeah, good point.

377
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,463
Well, don't get me wrong here

378
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:55,551
I do think being able to read a room
is an important skill.

379
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:58,427
But groups are made up of
different people.

380
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:02,099
It's rare for everyone to have exactly
the same thoughts and opinions.

381
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:03,892
That's because...

382
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:06,478
there's always people like me.

383
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:12,525
Big Bro,
are you sure you fit in at the shop?

384
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:13,569
Rude.

385
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,738
Love or hate. Good or evil.

386
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:18,865
So many opinions out there,

387
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:21,117
so decide for yourself what you believe.

388
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,285
Also,

389
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:24,162
you gotta start being more aware of it.

390
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,163
Aware?

391
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,499
Right. Of why you think that way.

392
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,834
If you don't understand yourself,

393
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:31,879
you'll never truly understand others.

394
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,132
Whoa, bro.

395
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:37,717
What happened to you after you left home?

396
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:40,345
Life happened to me and
it mellowed me out a bit.

397
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:43,724
399
- Ah.
- Okay, take care, man.

398
00:19:44,308 --> 00:19:47,269
Well, I mean as best as you can
when you're feeling crappy.

399
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:48,729
Kaito...

400
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:50,355
Come back soon, okay?

401
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:51,773
Sure.

402
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:54,443
I'll sneak in again to return the seal.

403
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:56,612
That's... not what I meant.

404
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:02,284
Was the motivation
behind everything I did

405
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:05,370
really just to avoid
turning out like my brother?

406
00:20:06,955 --> 00:20:07,873
No...

407
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,541
I couldn't understand why they

408
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:13,295
hated my brother so much and
treated him like they did.

409
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:15,672
I guess I was just... scared.

410
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:20,384
Always scanning the room and
feeling on edge trying to read everyone.

411
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:23,179
It wasn't me trying to label
others without knowing them...

412
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:25,306
or standing up against
peer pressure out of a

413
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:27,267
righteous sense of justice or anything.

414
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:31,188
It was cause I couldn't understand
where the hatred came from.

415
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:33,231
The ones who get pointed at.

416
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:34,191
The ones who point.

417
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:36,735
Me, who they're not pointing at for now.

418
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:39,613
The fine line between us
all was so arbitrary.

419
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:41,447
I just couldn't wrap

420
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:45,452
my head around all the malice and mockery
everyone was directing at one person.

421
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,662
I worried if I made a mistake,

422
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:51,290
there'd come a day when all the
fingers would point in my direction.

423
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,125
You're such a good kid,
unlike your brother.

424
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:56,046
- It makes things so much easier.
- What if...

425
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:58,465
I stopped being who I am now?

426
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:00,884
Big bro...

427
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,179
I'm sorry but I'm not
the kind person you think I am.

428
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:07,556
I'm not being considerate
for everyone else.

429
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:09,393
Or kind for kindness's sake.

430
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:12,520
I try to keep things harmonious...

431
00:21:12,521 --> 00:21:14,815
because I absolutely
can't stand the tension.

432
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:16,942
I reach out to help others...

433
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,652
cause if I ever ended up
in their position,

434
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:22,281
I'm terrified no one
would be there to help me.

435
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:25,826
I can't bring myself
to turn someone down...

436
00:21:26,576 --> 00:21:28,160
because I can't help imagining how

437
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:30,747
heartbreaking it would be
if I were in their shoes.

438
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:34,042
Despite what you
think, none of it's kindness.

439
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:37,670
It's just weakness...
because I don't want to be alone.

440
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:38,797
That's all it is.

441
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:44,803
I could never truly trust...
my family... my friends... anyone.

442
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:49,433
Or not enough to be vulnerable
and fully open myself up to them.

443
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:51,642
Minato,

444
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:53,978
you have a savior complex, that's why.

445
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,897
You want them to rely on you.

446
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:58,608
Ugh... Why now?

447
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:01,902
Words I thought I understood
the meaning of before,

448
00:22:01,903 --> 00:22:03,405
I'm actually starting to feel.

449
00:22:04,781 --> 00:22:07,075
I... I can't go on like this.

450
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:09,702
I can't truly open up to people.

451
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:10,954
I pretend I'm trying

452
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,123
only to end up hurting Momoka.

453
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,002
All I'm doing is just
using people for my own sake.

454
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:20,213
I can't...

455
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:22,841
I can't keep dating her like this.

